This is the Neuralese to English Translator: a compact-alphabet
reconstruction and fail-closed audit tool by Eric Buck (2026).

It learns a symbol pack from embeddings and/or text, glosses codes
into English, and certifies that live symbols stay addressable,
unfoldable, and checksum-bound.

It does not include the full Eris system, SLAR event-bus runtime,
identity/governance roots, or any model weights.

